php-vm calls proposal 0001: method and static call resolution (zend_std_get_method,
zend_std_get_static_method, ZEND_INIT_STATIC_METHOD_CALL). Base: 3be3cf4. Files: call.rs, exec.rs.

- zend_bad_method_call: "Call to private method A::m() from scope B" names the declaring class
  and the method name as written at the call (it used the object's class and the canonical name).
  Fixes tests/classes/private_003b, private_004, private_004b.
- get_static_method_fallback: `A::undefined()` from an instance context uses the `__call` of $this's
  class (the top-level one), not A's own. Fixes tests/classes/__call_004.
- Trampoline names stop at the first NUL byte (zend_get_call_trampoline_func).
  Fixes Zend/tests/magic_methods/bug46238.
- The abstract check also covers trampolines: an abstract `__callStatic` in an interface or abstract
  class gives "Cannot call abstract method Foo::bar()". Fixes magic_methods/gh_17718_001/002.
- `Calling static trait method T::m is deprecated, it should only be called on a class using the trait`.
- A literal `X::__construct()` calls the class constructor (op2 UNUSED): "Cannot call constructor"
  when there is none, and "Cannot call private X::__construct()" when $this's class is not the
  constructor's class. No other visibility check applies. Fixes magic_methods/call_static_006 and
  tests/classes/ctor_visibility.
- The InitStaticCall handler fetches the class before it reads the method name, so `$a::$b()`
  warns about $a and throws "Class name must be a valid object or a string".
  Fixes dynamic_call/dynamic_call_004.
- self::/parent:: forwarding takes the called scope from $this's class or the frame's called scope,
  as php-src does.

